# Build target. Two jobs:
#
#  1. Drop polyfills for features every current browser has. The ones
#     PageSpeed flagged (Array.at / .flat / .flatMap, Object.fromEntries,
#     Object.hasOwn, String.trimEnd) all shipped by Safari 15.4, so that's
#     the floor. ~14 KB of transpiled JS saved.
#
#  2. Not break older phones. The previous version of this file used
#     "last 2 Safari versions", which resolves to roughly Safari 18+ — that
#     silently drops support for every iPhone still on iOS 15, 16 or 17.
#     Those users would get untranspiled code with no polyfills. Chrome and
#     Edge auto-update so "last 2" is harmless there; Safari is tied to the
#     OS, so it needs an explicit floor.

chrome >= 100
edge >= 100
firefox >= 100
safari >= 15.4
ios_saf >= 15.4
samsung >= 19
not dead
